BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Use Gamification to Achieve Business Objectives - for Found
 ers and Newcomers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T190000
UID:69fbc3bd8e677a28001a5fc3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This interactive workshop equips startup and newcomer founders
  to harness gamification for business goals by influencing human behavior.
  Participants will learn core principles\, the 'Circle' framework\, and st
 rategies to overcome challenges using game mechanics. A relevant case stud
 y and collaborative discussion help craft tailored solutions\, followed by
  a Q&A to wrap-up the workshop for deeper insights.\n*The program's target
  age range is 18 and up (young adults/adults)\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 
 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd fl.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fbc3bd8e677a28001a5fc3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
