BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Visit: Antonio Nicaso
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T160000
UID:69fbb578177319280017eda6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Antonio Nicaso is a bestselling author\, an award-winning jour
 nalist\, a university professor\, and an internationally renowned expert o
 n organized crime. He has published over 50 books on Mafia and Mafia-type 
 organizations.  He is a regular consultant to governments and law-enforcem
 ent agencies around the world and is a lecturer at several universities.  
 In addition to sitting on advisory boards at prestigious educational insti
 tutions in Toronto and Rome\, he is also the President of Centro Scuola e 
 Cultura in Toronto.\n**Books will be read and discussed in Italian languag
 e.\nDrop in Program. No registration required.
LOCATION:Humber Summit\, Auditorium\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fbb578177319280017eda6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
