DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T153000
UID:69f22922fca21471b7f0a976@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Growing (and eating) your own vegetables has so many benefits.
  Come and discover the joy of growing your own food. You can’t beat the 
 taste\, and you save some money while doing it. We cover all the bases\, i
 ncluding planning new garden beds\, the importance of soil\, starting seed
 s indoors\, crop rotation\, caring for your plants\, feeding/fertilizing a
 nd maximizing productivity by extending the growing season.\nRegistration 
 Required.\nDrop-ins are welcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation Co
 llection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by th
 e Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\,
  20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progra
 m registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library 
 handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerlin
 e@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Discussion Room (located on the third
  floor).
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f22922fca21471b7f0a976
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
